# TLS front for the facilitator. Certificates are automatic (Let's Encrypt); the DNS record for
# this name must be DNS-only in Cloudflare (grey cloud) so the ACME challenge reaches Caddy.
#
# No rate limiting here on purpose: the stock caddy image does not ship the rate_limit module,
# and a directive it cannot parse would keep the whole front from starting. The facilitator
# authenticates every call itself (constant-time key check, 401 otherwise), which is the control
# that actually protects the fee balance. If junk traffic ever becomes a real cost, add
# Cloudflare proxying with an Origin Rule for ACME, or build Caddy with mholt/caddy-ratelimit.
facilitator.novacorplabs.com {
	reverse_proxy facilitator:8403
	encode gzip
}
